<article class="evd">

<h2>Shape and texture in the solar corona</h2>

<p class="evd-lede">
  A worked example run end to end through <strong>EVIE</strong> — segmentation,
  separable shape tensors, principal geodesic analysis, and a two-sample
  maximum-mean-discrepancy test. Every number and every curve on this page came
  out of the pipeline. Nothing here is illustrative.
</p>

<div class="evd-credit">
  Imagery courtesy of <strong>NASA/SDO</strong> and the AIA, EVE, and HMI
  science teams — <a href="https://sdo.gsfc.nasa.gov/">sdo.gsfc.nasa.gov</a>.
  Three AIA 193&nbsp;Å frames, 2048&nbsp;×&nbsp;2048, grouped by observation
  date.
</div>

<h3>The question</h3>

<p>
  Each frame segments into hundreds of closed level-set boundaries — the
  outlines of coronal structure. One image is therefore already an
  <em>ensemble</em> of shapes. Group the frames by date and a question follows
  naturally: <strong>does the distribution of coronal loop shapes change from
  one day to the next?</strong>
</p>

<p>
  A separable shape tensor splits each closed curve into two independent
  factors — a point on the Grassmannian <span class="evd-m">Gr(2,&nbsp;n)</span>
  carrying <em>undulation</em> (how the outline wiggles), and a
  symmetric-positive-definite matrix carrying <em>anisotropic scaling</em> (how
  big and how elongated it is). The test can then ask about each factor
  separately, and say <em>which kind</em> of difference it found.
</p>

<h3>Segmented boundaries</h3>

<p class="evd-note">
  The traced level sets, in image pixel coordinates. Colour marks the
  observation date. These are the actual curves the pipeline consumed.
</p>

<div class="evd-figure">
  <canvas id="evdCurves" height="420"></canvas>
  <div class="evd-legend" id="evdCurvesLegend"></div>
</div>

<h3>What the shape tensors say</h3>

<div class="evd-grid">
  <figure class="evd-panel">
    <figcaption>Grassmannian PGA spectrum</figcaption>
    <canvas id="evdSpec" height="200"></canvas>
    <p class="evd-cap">Singular values <span class="evd-m">σ<sub>k</sub></span>
      of the undulation factor, log scale. The decay says how many modes carry
      the ensemble's shape variation.</p>
  </figure>

  <figure class="evd-panel">
    <figcaption>Distance from the intrinsic mean</figcaption>
    <canvas id="evdScatter" height="200"></canvas>
    <p class="evd-cap">Each point is one boundary:
      <span class="evd-m">d<sub>Gr</sub></span> (undulation) against
      <span class="evd-m">d<sub>SPD</sub></span> (scaling), coloured by date.
      The two clouds overlap.</p>
  </figure>

  <figure class="evd-panel">
    <figcaption>Fréchet / Karcher mean</figcaption>
    <canvas id="evdMean" height="200"></canvas>
    <p class="evd-cap">The intrinsic mean shape (solid) over the standardized
      ensemble (faint). Computed on the manifold, not by averaging
      coordinates.</p>
  </figure>

  <figure class="evd-panel">
    <figcaption>Decision landscape</figcaption>
    <canvas id="evdDland" height="200"></canvas>
    <p class="evd-cap">Test outcome across the analysis grid — reduced
      dimension <span class="evd-m">r</span> against landmark count
      <span class="evd-m">n<sub>re</sub></span>. Circle = fail to reject,
      × = reject.</p>
  </figure>
</div>

<h3>The answer, and the interesting part</h3>

<p id="evdVerdict" class="evd-verdict"></p>

<p>
  A single run at one smoothing scale is a weak claim, so the pipeline sweeps
  the scale and re-runs the whole grid at each one. That is where this example
  stops being flat:
</p>

<div class="evd-figure">
  <canvas id="evdSweep" height="200"></canvas>
  <div class="evd-legend" id="evdSweepLegend"></div>
</div>

<p id="evdSweepText"></p>

<div class="evd-caveat">
  <strong>Read this before drawing a solar-physics conclusion.</strong>
  The two ensembles are <em>imbalanced</em> — <span id="evdN1"></span> boundaries
  from two frames on the first date against <span id="evdN2"></span> from a
  single frame on the second. The surviving boundary count also changes with
  smoothing scale, because smoothing decides which small structures clear the
  minimum-arc-length threshold. A decision that appears at one scale and not
  another is therefore evidence about <em>scale sensitivity of the statistic</em>,
  which is exactly what the sweep exists to expose — not, on this evidence, a
  measured change in the corona. Reporting it the other way round is the
  mistake the sweep is designed to prevent.
</div>

<h3>Reproducing this</h3>

<p>
  The dataset ships with the code as <code>data/sun_temporal/</code>, and this
  is one command:
</p>

<pre class="evd-pre"><code>evie-mmd-g2image --data-path data/sun_temporal \
    --r 5 10 20 --n-re 200 500 --scales 3 5 7</code></pre>

<p class="evd-note">
  EVIE also runs as an interactive terminal interface (<code>python -m evie</code>)
  and as a local dashboard, and mirrors the same pipeline in MATLAB/Octave.
  <span id="evdRepoLine"></span>
</p>

</article>



<script>
(function () {
  'use strict';
  const D = {{ evieDemo | dump | safe }};

  /* REPO_URL: set this to the public repository URL when `evie` goes public.
     See the front matter for the other two steps. */
  const REPO_URL = null;

  const css = n => getComputedStyle(document.documentElement)
                     .getPropertyValue(n).trim();
  const A = () => css('--color-accent-hover');
  const A2 = () => css('--color-text-secondary');
  const BORDER = () => css('--color-border');
  const TXT = () => css('--color-text-primary');

  const labels = [...new Set(D.samples.label)];
  const COL = () => [A(), '#b07d4a'];

  function fit(cv) {
    const dpr = window.devicePixelRatio || 1;
    const w = cv.clientWidth || 600, h = cv.height;
    cv.width = w * dpr; cv.style.height = h + 'px';
    cv.height = h * dpr;
    const ctx = cv.getContext('2d');
    ctx.setTransform(dpr, 0, 0, dpr, 0, 0);
    ctx.clearRect(0, 0, w, h);
    return [ctx, w, h];
  }

  function legend(el, names, cols) {
    el.innerHTML = names.map((n, i) =>
      `<span><span class="k" style="background:${cols[i]}"></span>${n}</span>`
    ).join('');
  }

  /* ---- traced boundaries ------------------------------------------------ */
  function drawCurves() {
    const cv = document.getElementById('evdCurves');
    const [ctx, W, H] = fit(cv);
    const cols = COL();
    // frames are square and identical in size; lay them side by side
    const frames = D.meta.frames;
    const n = frames.length;
    const pad = 8, cw = (W - pad * (n + 1)) / n;
    const side = Math.min(cw, H - pad * 2);
    frames.forEach((fr, i) => {
      const x0 = pad + i * (cw + pad) + (cw - side) / 2;
      const y0 = (H - side) / 2;
      ctx.strokeStyle = BORDER(); ctx.lineWidth = 1;
      ctx.strokeRect(x0, y0, side, side);
      const sc = side / fr.width;
      const ci = labels.indexOf(fr.label);
      ctx.strokeStyle = cols[ci % cols.length];
      ctx.lineWidth = 0.9;
      ctx.globalAlpha = 0.85;
      D.curves.filter(c => c.img === i).forEach(c => {
        ctx.beginPath();
        c.pts.forEach((p, j) => {
          const x = x0 + p[0] * sc, y = y0 + p[1] * sc;
          j ? ctx.lineTo(x, y) : ctx.moveTo(x, y);
        });
        ctx.closePath(); ctx.stroke();
      });
      ctx.globalAlpha = 1;
      ctx.fillStyle = A2();
      ctx.font = '10px ' + css('--font-mono');
      ctx.fillText(`${fr.label} · ${fr.n_shapes} shapes`, x0, y0 + side + 12);
    });
    legend(document.getElementById('evdCurvesLegend'), labels, cols);
  }

  /* ---- PGA spectrum ----------------------------------------------------- */
  function drawSpec() {
    const cv = document.getElementById('evdSpec');
    const [ctx, W, H] = fit(cv);
    const m = { l: 34, r: 10, t: 20, b: 22 };
    const v = D.spectrum.slice(0, 60).map(s => Math.max(s, 1e-12));
    const logs = v.map(Math.log10);
    const lo = Math.min(...logs), span = Math.max(Math.max(...logs) - lo, 1e-6);
    const iw = (W - m.l - m.r) / v.length;
    ctx.strokeStyle = BORDER();
    ctx.strokeRect(m.l, m.t, W - m.l - m.r, H - m.t - m.b);
    v.forEach((s, i) => {
      const h = Math.max(1, (H - m.t - m.b) * Math.max(0.02, (logs[i] - lo) / span));
      ctx.fillStyle = i < D.meta.r ? A() : BORDER();
      ctx.fillRect(m.l + i * iw, H - m.b - h, Math.max(1, iw * 0.7), h);
    });
    ctx.fillStyle = A2(); ctx.font = '9px ' + css('--font-mono');
    ctx.fillText('σ (log)', 2, 10);
    ctx.fillText(`k → (first ${v.length}; r = ${D.meta.r} retained)`, m.l, H - 6);
  }

  /* ---- distance scatter ------------------------------------------------- */
  function drawScatter() {
    const cv = document.getElementById('evdScatter');
    const [ctx, W, H] = fit(cv);
    const m = { l: 40, r: 10, t: 10, b: 26 };
    const x = D.samples.dSPD, y = D.samples.dGr;
    const xr = [Math.min(...x), Math.max(...x)], yr = [Math.min(...y), Math.max(...y)];
    const sx = v => m.l + (v - xr[0]) / (xr[1] - xr[0] || 1) * (W - m.l - m.r);
    const sy = v => H - m.b - (v - yr[0]) / (yr[1] - yr[0] || 1) * (H - m.t - m.b);
    ctx.strokeStyle = BORDER();
    ctx.strokeRect(m.l, m.t, W - m.l - m.r, H - m.t - m.b);
    const cols = COL();
    D.samples.label.forEach((l, i) => {
      ctx.fillStyle = cols[labels.indexOf(l) % cols.length];
      ctx.globalAlpha = 0.75;
      ctx.beginPath(); ctx.arc(sx(x[i]), sy(y[i]), 2.6, 0, 7); ctx.fill();
    });
    ctx.globalAlpha = 1;
    ctx.fillStyle = A2(); ctx.font = '9px ' + css('--font-mono');
    ctx.fillText('d_SPD  (scaling) →', m.l, H - 8);
    ctx.save(); ctx.translate(10, H / 2 + 26); ctx.rotate(-Math.PI / 2);
    ctx.fillText('d_Gr (undulation) →', 0, 0); ctx.restore();
  }

  /* ---- Karcher mean ----------------------------------------------------- */
  function drawMean() {
    const cv = document.getElementById('evdMean');
    const [ctx, W, H] = fit(cv);
    const all = [D.karcher.mean_shape, ...D.karcher.ensemble];
    let xs = [], ys = [];
    all.forEach(c => c.forEach(p => { xs.push(p[0]); ys.push(p[1]); }));
    const xr = [Math.min(...xs), Math.max(...xs)], yr = [Math.min(...ys), Math.max(...ys)];
    const pad = 14;
    const s = Math.min((W - 2 * pad) / (xr[1] - xr[0] || 1),
                       (H - 2 * pad) / (yr[1] - yr[0] || 1));
    const cx = (xr[0] + xr[1]) / 2, cy = (yr[0] + yr[1]) / 2;
    const px = v => W / 2 + (v - cx) * s, py = v => H / 2 - (v - cy) * s;
    const poly = (c) => {
      ctx.beginPath();
      c.forEach((p, i) => i ? ctx.lineTo(px(p[0]), py(p[1]))
                            : ctx.moveTo(px(p[0]), py(p[1])));
      ctx.closePath();
    };
    ctx.strokeStyle = A2(); ctx.lineWidth = 1; ctx.globalAlpha = 0.16;
    D.karcher.ensemble.forEach(c => { poly(c); ctx.stroke(); });
    ctx.globalAlpha = 1;
    poly(D.karcher.mean_shape);
    ctx.fillStyle = css('--color-accent-dim'); ctx.fill();
    ctx.strokeStyle = A(); ctx.lineWidth = 2; ctx.stroke();
    ctx.fillStyle = A2(); ctx.font = '9px ' + css('--font-mono');
    ctx.fillText(`intrinsic mean over N = ${D.karcher.n_samples}`, 8, H - 7);
  }

  /* ---- decision landscape ----------------------------------------------- */
  function drawDland() {
    const cv = document.getElementById('evdDland');
    const [ctx, W, H] = fit(cv);
    const dec = D.decisions;
    const R = dec.r_vals, N = dec.nre_vals, t = 0;      // gr channel
    const m = { l: 40, r: 12, t: 12, b: 26 };
    const cw = (W - m.l - m.r) / R.length, ch = (H - m.t - m.b) / N.length;
    ctx.font = '9px ' + css('--font-mono');
    for (let i = 0; i < R.length; i++) {
      for (let j = 0; j < N.length; j++) {
        const x = m.l + i * cw, y = m.t + j * ch;
        ctx.strokeStyle = BORDER(); ctx.strokeRect(x, y, cw, ch);
        const accept = dec.rslt[i][j][t] === 1;
        const mx = x + cw / 2, my = y + ch / 2;
        ctx.strokeStyle = accept ? A() : '#b0553f'; ctx.lineWidth = 1.8;
        if (accept) { ctx.beginPath(); ctx.arc(mx, my, 7, 0, 7); ctx.stroke(); }
        else {
          ctx.beginPath();
          ctx.moveTo(mx - 6, my - 6); ctx.lineTo(mx + 6, my + 6);
          ctx.moveTo(mx + 6, my - 6); ctx.lineTo(mx - 6, my + 6); ctx.stroke();
        }
      }
    }
    ctx.fillStyle = A2();
    R.forEach((r, i) => ctx.fillText(`r=${r}`, m.l + i * cw + 6, H - 10));
    N.forEach((n, j) => ctx.fillText(String(n), 6, m.t + j * ch + ch / 2 + 3));
    ctx.fillText('n_re', 6, m.t - 3);
  }

  /* ---- scale sweep ------------------------------------------------------ */
  function drawSweep() {
    const cv = document.getElementById('evdSweep');
    const [ctx, W, H] = fit(cv);
    const sw = D.sweep;
    const m = { l: 52, r: 14, t: 14, b: 30 };
    const nS = sw.scale_vals.length, nT = sw.tests.length;
    const cw = (W - m.l - m.r) / nS, ch = (H - m.t - m.b) / nT;
    ctx.font = '10px ' + css('--font-mono');
    for (let i = 0; i < nS; i++) {
      for (let j = 0; j < nT; j++) {
        const rej = sw.rejects[i][j], tot = sw.totals[i][j];
        const frac = tot ? rej / tot : 0;
        const x = m.l + i * cw, y = m.t + j * ch;
        ctx.fillStyle = frac > 0 ? '#b0553f' : css('--color-accent-dim');
        ctx.globalAlpha = frac > 0 ? 0.30 + 0.55 * frac : 0.55;
        ctx.fillRect(x, y, cw, ch);
        ctx.globalAlpha = 1;
        ctx.strokeStyle = BORDER(); ctx.strokeRect(x, y, cw, ch);
        ctx.fillStyle = TXT();
        ctx.fillText(`${rej}/${tot} reject`, x + 10, y + ch / 2 + 4);
      }
    }
    ctx.fillStyle = A2();
    sw.scale_vals.forEach((s, i) =>
      ctx.fillText(`scale ${s}`, m.l + i * cw + 10, H - 12));
    sw.tests.forEach((t, j) => {
      const nm = t === 'gr' ? 'undulation' : 'scaling';
      ctx.fillText(nm, 2, m.t + j * ch + ch / 2 + 4);
    });
    legend(document.getElementById('evdSweepLegend'),
           ['fail to reject H₀', 'reject H₀'],
           [css('--color-accent-dim'), '#b0553f']);
  }

  /* ---- prose driven by the real numbers --------------------------------- */
  function fillText() {
    const counts = {};
    D.samples.label.forEach(l => counts[l] = (counts[l] || 0) + 1);
    document.getElementById('evdN1').textContent = counts[labels[0]];
    document.getElementById('evdN2').textContent = counts[labels[1]];

    const dec = D.decisions;
    let acc = 0, tot = 0;
    dec.rslt.forEach(a => a.forEach(b => b.forEach(v => { tot++; if (v === 1) acc++; })));
    document.getElementById('evdVerdict').textContent =
      `Across every point of the analysis grid — ${dec.r_vals.length} values of r, ` +
      `${dec.nre_vals.length} landmark counts, both factors, ${tot} tests in all — ` +
      `the test fails to reject the null in ${acc} of ${tot}. At this smoothing ` +
      `scale the two days are statistically indistinguishable in both shape factors.`;

    const sw = D.sweep;
    const hits = [];
    sw.scale_vals.forEach((s, i) => sw.tests.forEach((t, j) => {
      if (sw.rejects[i][j] > 0) hits.push(
        `at scale ${s} the ${t === 'gr' ? 'undulation' : 'scaling'} factor ` +
        `rejects in ${sw.rejects[i][j]} of ${sw.totals[i][j]} tests`);
    }));
    document.getElementById('evdSweepText').textContent = hits.length
      ? `The decision is not constant across scale: ${hits.join('; ')} — while ` +
        `every other scale accepts throughout. A result that survives only at ` +
        `one smoothing scale is a different claim from one that holds across all ` +
        `of them, and the sweep is what tells the two apart.`
      : `The decision is constant across every smoothing scale tested.`;

    document.getElementById('evdRepoLine').innerHTML = REPO_URL
      ? `Source and documentation: <a href="${REPO_URL}">${REPO_URL}</a>.`
      : `The source repository is being prepared for public release.`;
  }

  function drawAll() {
    drawCurves(); drawSpec(); drawScatter();
    drawMean(); drawDland(); drawSweep();
  }

  fillText();
  drawAll();
  addEventListener('resize', drawAll);
  const themeBtn = document.getElementById('theme-toggle');
  if (themeBtn) themeBtn.addEventListener('click', () => setTimeout(drawAll, 60));
})();
</script>
